e. It was also more lightweight, which meant it was easier to transport, and it was much cheaper to produce than its German counterpart. A total of 6,884 ML-20’s were produced.","LocalizedString":"The 152 mm howitzer-gun M1937, also known as ML-20, was a Soviet heavy howitzer gun that was produced from 1937 to 1947 and used by the Red Army during WWII. The gun was one of the most successful Soviet artillery pieces during WWII as it had better range than the 15 cm sFH 18 German heavy howitzer, which meant that it could fire from positions where it was immune to enemy artillery fire. It was also more lightweight, which meant it was easier to transport, and it was much cheaper to produce than its German counterpart. A total of 6,884 ML-20’s were produced."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Legions","isInPermanentPool":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Destruction"],"hasDestruction":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Artillery_Move_FX'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Artillery_Move_FX.0"},"soundMoveToFrontline":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Artillery_Move_FX'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Artillery_Move_FX.0"},"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'explosion_large_01'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/ExplosionSoundPack/ExplosionSounds/Wavs/explosion_large_01.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Soviet/Invasion/t_152mm.t_152mm","SubPathString":""},"artist":"1939 Games","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/152mm_HOWITZER_GUN.152mm_HOWITZER_GUN","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":346.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_152mm_howitzer_gun_photo","SourceString":"Red Army artillery crew firing from a 152mm howitzer gun, Eastern Front, 1944.","LocalizedString":"Red Army artillery crew firing from a 152mm howitzer gun, Eastern Front, 1944."},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"Ob